<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spanish American wars of independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1808–1826</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Spanish-American independence wars</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Spanish American wars of independence were the conflicts from 1808 to 1826 in which most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s American colonies won independence. They were triggered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s invasion of Spain. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> treat them as the end of Spanish rule over most of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spanish-american-wars-of-independence.jpg" alt="Spanish American wars of independence" width="292" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ricardo Acevedo Bernal · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Congreso_de_C%C3%BAcuta.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section><h2 class="enc-section-title">Mentioned in 1 profile</h2><div class="enc-mentions"><a href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire<span class="secs">Decline</span></a></div></section>
